#: ../../../dev/intro.rst:164
msgid "Why are you being so hard on my pull request?"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../dev/intro.rst:166
msgid ""
"A pull request looks a little different depending on whether you're on the "
"\"contributor\" or \"maintainer\" side. The contributor says:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../dev/intro.rst:169
msgid "I implemented a new feature in your project for you!"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../dev/intro.rst:171
msgid "However, the maintainer hears:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../dev/intro.rst:173
msgid ""
"I wrote some code. I'd like you to test, support, document and maintain it "
"for me forever."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../dev/intro.rst:176
msgid ""
"The maintainer will want to make sure that the code is something we feel "
"comfortable taking that responsibility for. That means well tested, clear "
"implementation, fits into the overall architecture, etc."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../dev/intro.rst:180
msgid ""
"But perhaps the existing code doesn't fulfill this to start with; is it then "
"fair to expect it from a change in a pull request? For example asking for a "
"test or documentation, where there is none before. Well, the existing code "
"has some advantage just by being legacy;"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../dev/intro.rst:185
msgid ""
"Perhaps there isn't a test, but we know this code works because it's been "
"running in production for a long time without complaints. Then it's fair to "
"expect tests from code replacing it."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../dev/intro.rst:189
msgid ""
"Perhaps there isn't a test, and your code fixes a bug with the code. That "
"just highlights that there *should have been* a test to start with, and this "
"is the optimal time to add one."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../dev/intro.rst:193
msgid ""
"Perhaps how the code works (or what exactly it does) isn't clear to the "
"reviewer. A test will clarify and lock this down, and also prevent us from "
"*inadvertently breaking it later*."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../dev/intro.rst:197
msgid ""
"Another thing that the maintainer might be hard about is whether the code "
"actually solves the *entire* problem, or at least enough of it to stand on "
"its own. This will be more relevant to new features than bugfixes and "
"includes questions like;"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../dev/intro.rst:202
msgid ""
"Is the feature general enough to be used by other users? If not, do we "
"really need it or can it be implemented as part of something more general?"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../dev/intro.rst:206
msgid ""
"Is the feature completely implemented? That is, if a new feature is added it "
"should be available in the GUI, emit relevant trace information to enable "
"debugging, be correctly saved in the configuration, etc. If components of "
"this are missing, that's work the maintainer will have to do after accepting "
"the pull request."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../dev/intro.rst:212
msgid ""
"All in all, a great pull request creates less work for the maintainer, not "
"more."
msgstr ""
